{title: Rock of Ages Cleft for Me}
{key: C}
{time: 3/4}

{start_of_verse: 1}
Rock of [C]Ages, [<off>F</off>]cleft for [C]me, let me [G]hide myself in [C]Thee
Let the [G]water and the [C]blood, from Thy [G]wounded side which [C]flowed
Be of [C]sin the [<off>F</off>]double [C]cure; save from [**]wrath and [<off>G</off>]make me [C]pure.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 2}
Not the [C]labors [<off>F</off>]of my [C]hands, can ful[G]fill Thy law's de[C]mands
Could my [G]zeal no respite [C]know, could my [G]tears forever [C]flow
All for [C]sin could [<off>F</off>]not a[C]tone; Thou must [**]save, and [<off>G</off>]Thou a[C]lone.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
Nothing [C]in my [<off>F</off>]hand I [C]bring, simply [G]to the cross I [C]cling
Naked, [G]come to Thee for [C]dress; helpless, [G]look to Thee for [C]grace
Foul, I [C]to the [<off>F</off>]fountain [C]fly; wash me, [**]savior, [<off>G</off>]or I [C]die.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 4}
While I [C]draw this [<off>F</off>]fleeting [C]breath, when mine [G]eyes shall close in [C]death
When I [G]soar to worlds un[C]known, see Thee [G]on Thy judgment [C]throne
Rock of [C]Ages, [<off>F</off>]cleft for [C]me, let me [**]hide my[<off>G</off>]self in [C]Thee.
{end_of_verse}
